//www.indexventures.com/perspectives/taking-flight-our-investment-in-flapping-airplanes/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-01-28", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "Asher Spector;Flapping Airplanes", "score": 10, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "mark-xu", "insight": "Second, independent path to the same founders: Xu built a close tie to CEO Ben Spector through Prod, the student incubator Ben ran, which Index credits with the early shaping of Cursor, Mercor, Etched and Decart. Xu sits in that founder graph, not just one friendship.", "type": "relationship", "evidence_quote": "built a close relationship with Ben through the Prod community", "source_url": "https://www.indexventures.com/perspectives/taking-flight-our-investment-in-flapping-airplanes/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-01-28", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "high", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "Ben Spector;Prod;Cursor;Mercor;Etched;Decart", "score": 12, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "mark-xu", "insight": "Xu is new to Index: the Flapping process started 'not long after' he joined, so he joined before about January 2026 (no date published). He is tagged on the 2025-10-28 Fireworks post, but the tag may postdate the deal, so the bound cannot be narrowed. His first big early-stage lead came soon after he arrived from a growth seat.", "type": "timing", "evidence_quote": "Not long after Mark joined Index, Shardul was catching up with Chris Ré", "source_url": "https://www.indexventures.com/perspectives/taking-flight-our-investment-in-flapping-airplanes/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-01-28", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "high", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "Shardul Shah;Chris Ré", "score": 12, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "mark-xu", "insight": "How Xu signals conviction: the seed post quotes a text he sent Shah framing the decision as a visceral, founder-driven feeling rather than a model or price.", "type": "how-they-decide", "evidence_quote": "I can physically feel my excitement.", "source_url": "https://www.indexventures.com/perspectives/taking-flight-our-investment-in-flapping-airplanes/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-01-28", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "high", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "Shardul Shah", "score": 12, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "mark-xu", "insight": "Board seat sits with Xu, not senior partner Shah, and Index re-led the A itself nine months after the seed. Lux joined as co-lead but goes unmentioned in Index's post. Outsiders get allocation only alongside an insider re-lead.", "type": "timing", "evidence_quote": "lead their $1B million Series A, with Mark joining the board", "source_url": "https://www.indexventures.com/perspectives/toward-more-efficient-ai-leading-flapping-airplanes-1b-series-a/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-10-21", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "Lux Capital;Flapping Airplanes", "score": 10, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "mark-xu", "insight": "The Flapping thesis Xu signed is data-efficiency, not scale: a research bet that models can learn from far less data. That is the pre-training-research shape on my thesis.", "type": "contrarian-view", "evidence_quote": "today's models could be orders of magnitude more data-efficient than they are now", "source_url": "https://www.indexventures.com/perspectives/taking-flight-our-investment-in-flapping-airplanes/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-01-28", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "low", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "Flapping Airplanes", "score": 8, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "mark-xu", "insight": "Hone was a talent-graph referral: a friend flagged Moritz Stephan inside Cognition about a year before Index invested. The pattern is to track individuals inside hot AI companies before they leave.", "type": "deal-origin", "evidence_quote": "a friend introduced us to Moritz Stephan", "source_url": "https://www.indexventures.com/perspectives/ai-that-owns-business-outcomes-our-investment-in-hone/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-10-08", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "Moritz Stephan;Cognition;Benchmark", "score": 10, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "mark-xu", "insight": "Xu and Shah's application-layer thesis for AI-native automation: value goes to whoever owns the outcome layer above the model, not to task tools.", "type": "contrarian-view", "evidence_quote": "whoever owns the layer between the model and the enterprise", "source_url": "https://www.indexventures.com/perspectives/ai-that-owns-business-outcomes-our-investment-in-hone/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-10-08", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "Hone", "score": 10, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "mark-xu", "insight": "On Simile the Shah/Xu team was not first: A* co-led the seed, Index led the $100M A, then re-upped in Greenoaks' B. It is the same pattern as Flapping: lead once, then double down.", "type": "timing", "evidence_quote": "We first led Simile's Series A earlier this year", "source_url": "https://www.indexventures.com/perspectives/simulating-society-at-scale-our-investment-in-similes-200m-series-b/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-07-30", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "medium", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "medium", "derived_leads": "A*;Greenoaks;Joon Sung Park", "score": 8, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "martin-casado", "insight": "Casado frames GP title as the unlock for deal autonomy; non-GP Infra partners need a GP sponsor to commit", "type": "constraint", "evidence_quote": "Promoting Jennifer to general partner means that much more autonomy in deal making", "source_url": "https://techcrunch.com/2024/04/19/andreessen-horowitz-jennifer-li-125-billion-dollar-infrastructure-fund/", "source_type": "press", "source_date": "2024-04-19", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "Jennifer Li", "score": 10, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "martin-casado", "insight": "World Labs came from a ~20-year personal relationship; Li pitched them the world-model idea", "type": "deal-origin", "evidence_quote": "We've known World Labs cofounder Fei-Fei Li for nearly two decades.", "source_url": "https://a16z.com/announcement/investing-in-world-labs/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2024-09-13", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "Fei-Fei Li;Sarah Wang", "score": 10, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "martin-casado", "insight": "TypeSafe $870M Series A followed a long courtship of the founder; Andreessen and Horowitz co-signed, Casado took board", "type": "deal-origin", "evidence_quote": "We've long been fans of Diogo, the founder and CEO of TypeSafe", "source_url": "https://a16z.com/announcement/investing-in-typesafe-ai/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-10-09", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "Diogo Almeida;DCVC;Sequoia Capital", "score": 10, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "martin-casado", "insight": "Backs repeat founders: Phaze is the Parsec team again (a16z had Parsec board seat until Unity bought it)", "type": "deal-origin", "evidence_quote": "I'm very excited to be working with this team again", "source_url": "https://a16z.com/announcement/investing-in-phaze/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-11-04", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "medium", "derived_leads": "Benjy Boxer;Chris Dickson", "score": 9, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "martin-casado", "insight": "Says first checks are frontier investing; self-identifies as a productive (not financial) investor", "type": "how-they-decide", "evidence_quote": "nearly all first money in checks are frontier investing", "source_url": "https://a16z.com/the-evolving-landscape-of-venture-capital-mindsets/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-10-28", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "", "score": 10, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "martin-casado", "insight": "Bitter economics: AI converts capital into product, justifying very large early rounds", "type": "contrarian-view", "evidence_quote": "Systems that become more powerful the more data and money you pour into them.", "source_url": "https://a16z.com/bitter-economics/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2025-11-19", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "", "score": 10, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "martin-casado", "insight": "Will not reject AI apps on low gross margins alone (co-written with Sarah Wang)", "type": "contrarian-view", "evidence_quote": "Being a pessimist makes you sound smart. Being an optimist makes you money.", "source_url": "https://a16z.com/questioning-margins-is-a-boring-cliche/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2025-08-21", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "low", "lens_fit": "medium", "derived_leads": "Sarah Wang", "score": 7, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "martin-casado", "insight": "2026 thesis cluster: agents need full computers (Runta seed, Phaze, doxxnet, Relace)", "type": "how-they-decide", "evidence_quote": "But it's increasingly clear that AI agents just want a computer.", "source_url": "https://a16z.com/announcement/investing-in-runta/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-07-16", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "Runta;Phaze;doxxnet;Relace;Yoko Li;Guido Appenzeller", "score": 10, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "martin-casado", "insight": "Cursor: a16z led the $60M A at $400M (TechCrunch corrected Thrive co-lead); OpenAI Startup Fund led seed first", "type": "timing", "evidence_quote": "That round was led by a16z.", "source_url": "https://techcrunch.com/2024/12/19/in-just-4-months-ai-coding-assistant-cursor-raised-another-100m-at-a-2-5b-valuation-led-by-thrive-sources-say", "source_type": "press", "source_date": "2024-12-19", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "OpenAI Startup Fund;Thrive Capital", "score": 10, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "martin-casado", "insight": "Casado on Cursor board; quoted on adoption at the Thrive-led $105M round", "type": "relationship", "evidence_quote": "We've never seen a company achieve such broad and rapid adoption", "source_url": "https://www.maginative.com/article/anysphere-raises-105m-for-ai-coding-assistant-cursor-reaching-2-5b-valuation/", "source_type": "press", "source_date": "2025-01-14", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "low", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "Thrive Capital;Benchmark", "score": 8, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "martin-casado", "insight": "Co-author of $1.1B Machine Age Fund for chips, memory, networking, power: the a16z pool for AI semis", "type": "crux", "evidence_quote": "This fund will invest into all of the computer infrastructure on which AI runs", "source_url": "https://a16z.com/the-machine-age-fund/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-08-28", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "low", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "Ben Horowitz;Raghu Raghuram;David Ulevitch;David George", "score": 8, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "martin-mignot", "insight": "Beside came from a 12-year friendship: Mignot met founder Maxime Germain in 2012 at a friend's TriBeCa startup loft and wrote a personal pre-seed check before Index led the seed.", "type": "deal-origin", "evidence_quote": "I invested personally in Beside's pre-seed round", "source_url": "https://www.indexventures.com/perspectives/beside/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2025-11-11", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "high", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "Maxime Germain;Kenneth Schlenker;Beside", "score": 12, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "martin-mignot", "insight": "Mignot's edge is being the first believer through long founder relationships; Deliveroo's CEO says so on Index's team page.", "type": "crux", "evidence_quote": "Martin was the first investor to believe in us.", "source_url": "https://www.indexventures.com/team/martin-mignot/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "low", "lens_fit": "medium", "derived_leads": "Will Shu;Deliveroo", "score": 7, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "martin-mignot", "insight": "Compute thesis: AI scaling's binding cost is energy, which justified backing Phaidra (AI data-center cooling). But Index entered ~2 years after first institutional money (2022 round; Helena A) per https://www.phaidra.ai/news.", "type": "timing", "evidence_quote": "Compute is king.", "source_url": "https://www.indexventures.com/perspectives/compute-is-king-our-investment-in-phaidra/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2024-07-02", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "medium", "derived_leads": "Phaidra;Helena;Collaborative Fund;Jim Gao", "score": 9, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "martin-mignot", "insight": "Why AI-native services over SaaS: in messy physical industries, rule-based software fails, so he backs human-plus-agent firms like Build.", "type": "contrarian-view", "evidence_quote": "Deterministic software breaks down at the edges", "source_url": "https://www.indexventures.com/perspectives/automating-the-built-world-our-partnership-with-build/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-06-29", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "low", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "Build;James Stirrat-Ellis;Ben McClusky", "score": 8, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "martin-mignot", "insight": "Founder filter: favors founders immersed at the AI frontier, even when targeting unglamorous small businesses.", "type": "how-they-decide", "evidence_quote": "The best founders today live and breathe at the frontier", "source_url": "https://www.indexventures.com/perspectives/beside/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2025-11-11", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "low", "lens_fit": "medium", "derived_leads": "Beside", "score": 7, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "martin-mignot", "insight": "Rimer named Mignot among Index's next generation of leaders (with Shah, Achadjian, Hammer); Mignot is a French investor based in NY close to Rimer.", "type": "relationship", "evidence_quote": "la próxima generación de líderes", "source_url": "https://www.bloomberglinea.com/mercados/index-ventures-el-silencioso-hacedor-de-reyes-de-silicon-valley-busca-sucesores/", "source_type": "press", "source_date": "2026-01-08", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "medium", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "medium", "derived_leads": "Danny Rimer;Shardul Shah;Nina Achadjian;Jan Hammer", "score": 8, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "masayoshi-son", "insight": "Son is named as a decision-maker on OpenAI only while the deal sat on the parent. For the 2025 round (investing entity 'SBG or its subsidiary') final terms went to Son and Goto. For the 2026 $30B, booked to Vision Fund 2 from the start, they went to Goto alone. Son owns 17.25% of that fund's co-investment equity. That this is why he stepped out is my inference; no filing says so.", "type": "how-they-decide", "evidence_quote": "was delegated to Mr. Masayoshi Son", "source_url": "https://group.softbank/en/news/press/20250401", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2025-04-01", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "medium", "derived_leads": "Yoshimitsu Goto", "score": 9, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "masayoshi-son", "insight": "Son says Altman asked him for $10B before 2019 and he agreed; OpenAI chose Microsoft. So the 2024-26 buying is a second attempt at a deal he lost, at a far higher price. The path was founder to Son directly, not through the fund.", "type": "deal-origin", "evidence_quote": "eventually, they picked Microsoft", "source_url": "https://www.nbcdfw.com/news/business/money-report/softbank-ceo-says-hes-all-in-on-openai-reveals-hes-long-wanted-microsofts-spot-as-main-backer/3873283/", "source_type": "press", "source_date": "2025-06-27", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "medium", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "medium", "derived_leads": "Sam Altman", "score": 8, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "masayoshi-son", "insight": "Why Son missed the labs when they were cheap: a former Vision Fund executive says the money was already spread across five or six hundred companies by 2021-22. The lesson he drew is concentration, which is why the AI book is now one position.", "type": "mistake", "evidence_quote": "he had used all his ammunition on other companies", "source_url": "https://newsio.com/2025/08/11/softbank-founder-son-makes-his-biggest-bet-by-staking-the-japanese-giants-future-on-ai/", "source_type": "press", "source_date": "2025-08-11", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "medium", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "medium", "derived_leads": "Alok Sama", "score": 8, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "masayoshi-son", "insight": "Under Alex Clavel, Vision Fund 2 passed on both OpenAI and Anthropic over valuation (Reuters, January 2024). Nine months later Son bought OpenAI at $157B and has since paid up to $730B. The fund's price discipline did not survive his conviction.", "type": "mistake", "evidence_quote": "passing on high-profile AI investment opportunities, such as OpenAI and Anthropic", "source_url": "https://ca.finance.yahoo.com/news/behind-softbank-investing-cleanup-us-110626656.html", "source_type": "press", "source_date": "2024-01-11", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "medium", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "medium", "derived_leads": "Alex Clavel", "score": 8, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "masayoshi-son", "insight": "Son funds conviction by selling other winners, not by raising outside money. He sold all of SoftBank's NVIDIA shares in October 2025 to pay for OpenAI and said he would have kept them if he had the cash.", "type": "constraint", "evidence_quote": "I was crying to sell Nvidia shares", "source_url": "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/dont-want-sell-single-share-002214711.html", "source_type": "press", "source_date": "2025-12-02", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "medium", "non_obvious": "low", "lens_fit": "low", "derived_leads": "Jensen Huang", "score": 5, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "masayoshi-son", "insight": "Son's own map of what he buys: models, semiconductors, AI infrastructure and robots, which he calls the four corners of an Othello board. A chip, compute or robotics company sits inside it as a possible acquisition; an AI application does not.", "type": "crux", "evidence_quote": "Once you secure the four corners in the middle of the game", "source_url": "https://group.softbank/en/ir/financials/annual_reports/2026/message/son", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-06-24", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "medium", "derived_leads": "", "score": 9, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "masayoshi-son", "insight": "The frontier-model corner is already filled. Son names OpenAI as the group's partner for models in his 2026 letter, and no other lab appears in any SoftBank pool. A new lab should not expect Son as its anchor.", "type": "constraint", "evidence_quote": "Our key partner in the AI model area, which governs intelligence, is OpenAI", "source_url": "https://group.softbank/en/ir/financials/annual_reports/2026/message/son", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-06-24", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "high", "derived_leads": "OpenAI", "score": 10, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "masayoshi-son", "insight": "Yet he does not describe the model market as winner-take-all. The day before the 2026 shareholders' meeting he said OpenAI, Anthropic and Google all have room to grow many times over (Bloomberg paraphrase with a partial quote).", "type": "contrarian-view", "evidence_quote": "ten-fold, a hundred-fold", "source_url": "https://www.swissinfo.ch/eng/softbanks-masayoshi-son-scraps-plan-to-retire-in-his-sixties/91638621", "source_type": "press", "source_date": "2026-06-24", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "medium", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "medium", "derived_leads": "Anthropic", "score": 8, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "masayoshi-son", "insight": "No succession on the horizon. At 68 Son dropped his plan to hand over in his sixties and asked shareholders for another 10 or 15 years. Whoever wants SoftBank's largest checks deals with him into the 2030s.", "type": "timing", "evidence_quote": "I don’t have time to retire", "source_url": "https://www.swissinfo.ch/eng/softbanks-masayoshi-son-scraps-plan-to-retire-in-his-sixties/91638621", "source_type": "press", "source_date": "2026-06-24", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "medium", "non_obvious": "low", "lens_fit": "low", "derived_leads": "", "score": 5, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "masayoshi-son", "insight": "Son has rewritten his own published life plan to fit the AI bet. The plan he drew up at 19 had him handing over in his sixties; the 2026 letter replaces that with building superintelligence in his seventies.", "type": "how-they-decide", "evidence_quote": "I have decided to update my 50-year life plan", "source_url": "https://group.softbank/en/ir/financials/annual_reports/2026/message/son", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-06-24", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "low", "lens_fit": "low", "derived_leads": "", "score": 6, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "masayoshi-son", "insight": "Son sizes commitments to match his counterparty's appetite, in public. He doubled his 2016 US pledge to $100B at Mar-a-Lago in December 2024; Stargate followed five weeks later with him as chairman.", "type": "relationship", "evidence_quote": "President Trump is a double-down president", "source_url": "https://semafor.com/article/12/17/2024/softbank-ceo-son-pledges-100b-in-us-projects-to-trump", "source_type": "press", "source_date": "2024-12-18", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "medium", "non_obvious": "low", "lens_fit": "skip", "derived_leads": "Lionel Barber", "score": 4, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "masayoshi-son", "insight": "Son treats a missing check as the only real risk. On OpenAI he told shareholders the company will list and become the most valuable in the world, and framed the question as courage, not price.", "type": "how-they-decide", "evidence_quote": "takes bravery to invest", "source_url": "https://www.nbcdfw.com/news/business/money-report/softbank-ceo-says-hes-all-in-on-openai-reveals-hes-long-wanted-microsofts-spot-as-main-backer/3873283/", "source_type": "press", "source_date": "2025-06-27", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "medium", "non_obvious": "low", "lens_fit": "low", "derived_leads": "", "score": 5, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "matchvc", "insight": "Initial tickets are €200k to €1M, pre-seed to seed, from a €49M Fund I; structurally a sub-$10M-check fund.", "type": "check-size", "evidence_quote": "Our initial tickets range from €200k up to €1M", "source_url": "https://www.maetch.vc/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-11-10", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "low", "lens_fit": "low", "derived_leads": "", "score": 6, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "matchvc", "insight": "They prefer to move via convertible loan agreements (CLAs) to win on speed, often before incorporation, but will lead or follow priced rounds.", "type": "how-they-decide", "evidence_quote": "Because speed is crucial, we prefer moving fast via CLAs", "source_url": "https://www.maetch.vc/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-11-10", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "low", "derived_leads": "", "score": 8, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "matchvc", "insight": "Fund I final close at €49M from 91 LPs against a €35M target (July 2025); the BW Pre-Seed page still says €48M and 70 LPs, so that page looks stale.", "type": "lp-mechanics", "evidence_quote": "Final Closing: €49M Raised from 91 Strategic LPs - Surpassing €35M Target", "source_url": "https://www.maetch.vc/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2025-07", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "low", "derived_leads": "", "score": 8, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "matchvc", "insight": "Explicit anti-list: no GPT wrappers, chemistry, medtech, biotech, pharma, B2C or food; markets must exceed €1B TAM; no solo founders.", "type": "constraint", "evidence_quote": "Boring GPT wrappers, chemistry, medtech, or anything that lacks vision", "source_url": "https://www.maetch.vc/bwpreseed", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2025", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "low", "derived_leads": "", "score": 8, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "matchvc", "insight": "Runs a state-subsidised pre-seed lane: co-invests €40k next to L-Bank's €160k convertible loan in Start-up BW Pre-Seed for Baden-Württemberg teams.", "type": "check-size", "evidence_quote": "€40,000 from us as your co-investor", "source_url": "https://www.maetch.vc/bwpreseed", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2025", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "low", "derived_leads": "L-Bank", "score": 8, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "vector-informatik", "insight": "An LP's own operating company co-invested directly in Black Forest Labs next to a16z, alongside Mätch: Vector founder Helmut Schelling says so on Mätch's site.", "type": "relationship", "evidence_quote": "Our co-investment with a16z in Black Forest Labs proves it.", "source_url": "https://www.maetch.vc/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-11-10", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "medium", "derived_leads": "Helmut Schelling;Vector Informatik;Black Forest Labs;Andreessen Horowitz", "score": 9, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "matchvc", "insight": "Mätch was set up by the Gründermotor (now NXTGN) startup initiative, which also holds shares in the fund manager/fund, to give its best teams follow-on money.", "type": "lp-mechanics", "evidence_quote": "an dem Gründermotor auch Anteile hält", "source_url": "https://join-nxtgn.com/about/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2023-06", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "high", "non_obvious": "medium", "lens_fit": "low", "derived_leads": "NXTGN;Adrian Thoma;Helmut Schelling", "score": 8, "sig": 0}, {"subject_slug": "matchvc", "insight": "L-Bank (Baden-Württemberg state bank) describes itself as having launched Mätch VC as an anchor investor; wording is ambiguous whether L-Bank is the anchor LP.", "type": "lp-mechanics", "evidence_quote": "einen tollen Player als Ankerinvestor an den Start gebracht", "source_url": "https://join-nxtgn.com/", "source_type": "firm-site", "source_date": "2026-11-10", "timestamp_in_source": "", "confidence": "med